SUMMARY: The normative protections and implementation ownership are coherent, but the file-budget rule contradicts the actual driver and does not cover this complete candidate consistently.
REVIEWER: Codex, GPT-6-family agent in fresh review context; exact serving model variant is not exposed to this reviewer. Independent document/code review, not external human anonymity-systems review. No delegation. Read-only shell/Python inspection except this verdict. No runtime implementation, browser packet capture, Docker/live execution, or external protocol validation was performed by this reviewer.
SCOPE: target/T156/amendment.diff and its 88-input manifest, old constitution and before-turn documents, T156 acceptance, authoritative workflow and affected source/contract context. Implementer rationale/constitution-amendment-plan.md content, prior reviews/findings and SECURITY-DECISIONS.md were not read. The rationale file was hash-checked as a manifest input only.
FINDINGS:
  - [Major] docs/process/ticket-template.md:22 — The active template excludes the ticket itself and all specs/ files from files_budget, while the canonical driver counts every changed path; T156 declares 24 for a candidate with 88 changed documents. Checklist 2 / Acceptance 3 and 5.
    WRONG: This exact candidate is 15 <= 24 under the template exclusion, but 88 > 24 under the driver's raw-file rule; calling it within budget cannot establish normal reviewed delivery under both.
    EXPECTED: One explicit counting rule shared by the template, review report and actual driver, with a declared budget covering the complete authorized amendment scope.
    EVIDENCE: docs/process/ticket-template.md:20-22 defines the exclusion; scripts/run-task.sh:460-465 extracts the full git-diff file count and emits OVER BUDGET without a specs exclusion; docs/process/workflow.md:315 makes exceeding the budget a bright-line condition. T156 frontmatter at specs/001-tor-route/tickets/T156-strengthen-constitution-and-reconcile-plan.md:12 is 24. All 88 manifest paths differ from the supplied before-turn state; 15 are outside specs.
    FALSIFICATION ATTEMPT: Checked whether the driver implements the template exclusion, whether manifest entries merely repeat unchanged context, and whether the amendment declares an explicit alternate budget. It does none of these. The parent confirmed the conflicting rules should be reconciled and supplied no exemption; the candidate stayed unchanged.
    SURVIVAL: The template exclusion explains the reported 15-file count but does not reconcile the contradictory deterministic gate. This is a document/workflow consistency defect, not a claim that the requested reconciliation is unauthorized or unrelated.
    FIX: Align the template with the actual complete-path counting rule and declare a bounded T156 budget for the full reviewed amendment, including tracked/untracked documents and necessary durable delivery records. Refresh the exact manifest and verification evidence; do not hide specs paths or silently expand the reviewed scope.
    EVALUATED-AS: Recompute the scoped changed-path count from the renewed manifest against the stated review base and assert it is <= T156 files_budget; inspect docs/process/ticket-template.md:20-22 to confirm the specs/ticket exclusion is removed or reconciled with the driver. The normal driver report must use that same count and show no over-budget condition. New paths must trace to T156 acceptance or this finding.

